WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.000
This is a production of Cornell
University. Hi my name is Karen Luong and

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.170
I'm a transfer junior at the School of
Integrative Plant Science, also known as

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:13.160
SIPS. I'm mostly interested in 
plant pathology and that interest

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.910
started in high school, where I took many
agricultural classes including

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.380
horticulture and in my horticulture
class two graduate students at the New

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.650
York State Agricultural Experiment
Station came in with rotting fruit and

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.060
veggies and diseased plants and they
taught my class how to identify common

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:33.680
diseases of plants and how to manage
them. Senior year I had the opportunity

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.600
of interning at the Experiment Station
with a plant pathologist for a couple of

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.640
days and I ran basic tests like gel
electrophoresis I learned how to

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:49.520
sequence DNA and even inoculated beans
with white mold. I talked to the plant

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:57.140
pathologists about why doing research is
important and they told me that they do

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.660
research to recommend disease management
practices for farmers and they're part

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.100
of the solution for food security, and
ever since that day I've decided to

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.549
pursue a career in plant pathology. I've
always wanted to come to Cornell

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:17.180
probably because my agriculture teacher is an alumna and I've done internships

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:23.240
that's at the station and the researchers I
worked under are both professors at SIPS

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:28.939
and they've influenced my decision to
come study here but I went to community

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:32.479
college first for two years. However my transition from community

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:38.420
college to SIPS has been really smooth
and I appreciate how the Plant Sciences

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.430
program here includes
a wide array of concentrations like

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.470
Plant Pathology and the courses within
the concentrations can be very specific

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:52.820
like fungal genomics and as a plant
science student I'm able to take courses

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.930
in other concentrations like plant
genetics and breeding and sustainable

00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:02.540
plant production. Also the faculty and
students here at SIPS are supportive and

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:06.829
collaborative and there's many research
opportunities here on campus. So if

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:10.410
you're interested in plant
science I highly encourage you to see

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.360
what sips and Cornell has to offer.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:27.840
This has been a production of Cornell
University on the web at cornell.edu

